# ═══ Feature stages (kit.notes.md 2026-10-19 08:23Z) ═════════════════════════
# "a board view which enforces the feature creation pipeline. Let's make this
# separate from the existing board for now and we can unify them later if it
# makes sense before public release". Ids are STAGE, not PIPELINE: snip-it.beh
# already has a FEAT-PIPELINE for its video board, and one word meaning two
# boards a corpus apart is the trap the BEH-UI note above describes.
#
# A feature's stage lives in the corpus as `stage <problem|ux|logic|development|ui>`
# under its `feature` line: a corpus LANGUAGE change (claude-code-bot#58), which he
# approved on BEH-STAGE-1 at 2026-10-19 13:39Z. Built: BEH-STAGE-1 and -3. Still
# pending: what "written" means for a stage (BEH-STAGE-2) and the agent's halves.

feature FEAT-STAGES "Feature stages"
  stage development

behaviour BEH-STAGE-1 "A separate board takes every feature through five stages: problem, UX, logic, development, UI"
  in FEAT-STAGES
  source defined kit.notes.md#2026-10-19-0823
  priority 2
  review approved
  actor engineer
  when opens page:KitStages
  then sees region:KitStagesBoard
  contract the stages, in order: problem statement, UX requirements, business logic, development, UI requirements
  contract separate from the behaviour board (FEAT-BOARD) for now; unifying the two is a later call, before a public release
  contract a column per stage, a card per feature, coloured by project as the behaviour board's are

behaviour BEH-STAGE-2 "Every feature goes through the stages; a simple one just needs less written at each"
  in FEAT-STAGES
  source defined kit.notes.md#2026-10-19-0823
  priority 2
  pending
  actor engineer
  when opens page:KitStages
  then sees region:KitStagesBoard
  contract the stages are required, not reserved for complex features; a one-line answer at a stage is enough
  contract a feature moves on only when the stage it is in has been written

behaviour BEH-STAGE-3 "Development is iterative and runs through the spec: behaviours are added and refined until they are built"
  in FEAT-STAGES
  source defined kit.notes.md#2026-10-19-0823
  priority 3
  actor engineer
  when opens page:KitStages
  then sees region:KitStagesBoard
  contract a feature in development shows its behaviours' progress, built out of total, from the same counts the project page uses

